{"abstract":[{"text":"Trees over a sequence of values or a set of intervals that answer range queries and take updates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in O(log ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Fenwick trees","anchor":"Fenwick-trees","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/FenwickTree"]},{"title":"Segment trees","anchor":"Segment-trees","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree"]},{"title":"Interval trees","anchor":"Interval-trees","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree"]},{"title":"Monoids","anchor":"Monoids","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Monoid","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Sum","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Product","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Minimum","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Maximum","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction"]},{"title":"Extended Modules","generated":true,"anchor":"Extended-Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Trees"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"title":"RangeTrees","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"RangeTrees"}],"role":"collection","externalID":"RangeTrees","roleHeading":"Framework"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/FenwickTree"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps the prefix sums of a sequence of values in one flat array of partial"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sums. Prefix sums, range sums and point updates each touch O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") cells, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/FenwickTree\/lowerBound(ofPrefixSum:)"},{"type":"text","text":" finds where a running total crosses a value by binary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lifting."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import RangeTrees","","var scores: FenwickTree = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6]","scores.prefixSum(through: 3)        \/\/ 9","scores.sum(in: 2 ..< 6)             \/\/ 19","scores.add(10, at: 1)","scores.lowerBound(ofPrefixSum: 15)  \/\/ 2"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A Fenwick tree’s update tree, in which each cell’s parent is the next cell an add reaches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"converts to Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arborescence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arborescence(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (import Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trees","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module beside this one), so Grafluent’s tree algorithms and drawings run over it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" combines any range of values under a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Monoid","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": an associative operation with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an identity, written as a type such as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Sum","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Minimum","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" or one of your own, which need not be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"commutative. Range queries and point updates take O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree\/maxRight(from:where:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree\/minLeft(upTo:where:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" find how far a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range can grow while a monotone condition on it holds."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var heights = SegmentTree<Maximum<Int>>([3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6])","heights.combined(in: 0 ..< 4)        \/\/ 4","heights.update(at: 1, to: 7)","heights.maxRight(from: 0) { $0 < 9 } \/\/ 5"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree","isActive":true},{"text":" also applies an update to every value in a range in O(log ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":"), leaving it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pending at the cells that cover the range. A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction","isActive":true},{"text":" names the monoid, the updates and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"how an update changes a combined value; it is told how many values the combination covers, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adding a constant to a range of sums is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sum + update * count"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" holds half-open intervals with a value each, in an AVL tree ordered by lower"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bound whose vertices also record the largest upper bound below them. It finds the intervals that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"contain a point, overlap a range or lie within one, skipping every subtree that ends too early."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var bookings = IntervalTree<Int, String>()","bookings.insert(9 ..< 11, value: \"Ada\")","bookings.insert(10 ..< 12, value: \"Grace\")","bookings.containing(10).map(\\.value)          \/\/ [\"Ada\", \"Grace\"]","bookings.overlapping(11 ..< 13).map(\\.value)  \/\/ [\"Grace\"]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The segment trees’ and the interval tree’s shapes convert to Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree"},{"type":"text","text":" with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/rangetrees"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://RangeTrees/documentation/RangeTrees/MonoidAction":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MonoidAction","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Updates that act on the values of a monoid, for ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": a monoid of updates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under composition, each mapping a combined value of a run of elements to the combined value","type":"text"},{"